examples.question_text:
A rectangular prism has a base measuring $9\text{ cm}$ by $12\text{ cm}$ and a perpendicular height of $6\text{ cm}$. Its space diagonal joins a base vertex $A$ to the opposite top vertex $T$, directly above base vertex $C$.
Find, to 1 decimal place:
a. the angle that $AT$ makes with the base;
b. the angle that $AT$ makes with the vertical edge $CT$.
The two relevant triangles are shown separately.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (3,0);\coordinate (C) at (3,2);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;\draw (2.75,0)--(2.75,0.25)--(3,0.25);
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$} (B) node[below right] {$B$} (C) node[above right] {$C$};
\path (1.5,0) node[below] {$9\text{ cm}$} (3,1) node[right] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\begin{scope}[xshift=5cm]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (C) at (3,0);\coordinate (T) at (3,1.8);
\draw (A)--(C)--(T)--cycle;\draw (2.75,0)--(2.75,0.25)--(3,0.25);
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$} (C) node[below right] {$C$} (T) node[above right] {$T$};
\path (1.5,0) node[below] {$AC$} (3,0.9) node[right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A square pyramid has base side $10\text{ cm}$. Its apex $T$ lies vertically above the centre $C$ of the base, with $TC=5\text{ cm}$. Let $M$ be the midpoint of a base edge and $Q$ one endpoint of that edge.
Find, to 1 decimal place:
a. the angle between that side face and the base;
b. the angle between the slant edge $TQ$ and the base.
These are the perpendicular sections used for the two angles.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (M) at (0,0);\coordinate (C) at (2.5,0);\coordinate (T) at (2.5,2.5);
\draw (M)--(C)--(T)--cycle;\draw (2.25,0)--(2.25,0.25)--(2.5,0.25);
\path (M) node[below left] {$M$} (C) node[below right] {$C$} (T) node[above right] {$T$};
\path (1.25,0) node[below] {$CM$} (2.5,1.25) node[right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\begin{scope}[xshift=5cm]
\coordinate (Q) at (0,0);\coordinate (C) at (3,0);\coordinate (T) at (3,2.2);
\draw (Q)--(C)--(T)--cycle;\draw (2.75,0)--(2.75,0.25)--(3,0.25);
\path (Q) node[below left] {$Q$} (C) node[below right] {$C$} (T) node[above right] {$T$};
\path (1.5,0) node[below] {$CQ$} (3,1.1) node[right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rectangular prism has length $14\text{ cm}$, depth $6\text{ cm}$ and height $6\text{ cm}$. A diagonal plane contains the front bottom edge and the parallel back top edge.
Find the angle that this plane makes with the base, to the nearest degree.
The section below is perpendicular to the front bottom edge. Here $A$ is on that edge, $D$ is directly behind $A$ on the base, and $H$ is directly above $D$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (D) at (3,0);\coordinate (H) at (3,3);
\draw (A)--(D)--(H)--cycle;\draw (2.75,0)--(2.75,0.25)--(3,0.25);
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$} (D) node[below right] {$D$} (H) node[above right] {$H$};
\path (1.5,0) node[below] {$6\text{ cm}$} (3,1.5) node[right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A vertical tower $TC$ is $60\text{ m}$ tall on level ground. Observer $A$ is due south of $C$, and observer $B$ is due east of $C$. Their angles of elevation of $T$ are $45^\circ$ and $30^\circ$, respectively.
Find $AB$ to the nearest metre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (C) at (2,0);\coordinate (T) at (2,2);
\draw (A)--(C)--(T)--cycle;\draw (1.75,0)--(1.75,0.25)--(2,0.25);
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$} (C) node[below right] {$C$} (T) node[above right] {$T$};
\path (2,1) node[right] {$60\text{ m}$} (0.65,0.25) node {$45^\circ$};
\begin{scope}[xshift=4.5cm]
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);\coordinate (C) at (3,0);\coordinate (T) at (3,1.8);
\draw (B)--(C)--(T)--cycle;\draw (2.75,0)--(2.75,0.25)--(3,0.25);
\path (B) node[below left] {$B$} (C) node[below right] {$C$} (T) node[above right] {$T$};
\path (3,0.9) node[right] {$60\text{ m}$} (0.75,0.2) node {$30^\circ$};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Find the two ground distances using the elevation triangles.
$\begin{align*}\tan45^\circ&=\frac{60}{AC}\\AC&=\frac{60}{\tan45^\circ}\\AC&=60\text{ m}\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}\tan30^\circ&=\frac{60}{BC}\\BC&=\frac{60}{\tan30^\circ}\\BC&=60\sqrt{3}\text{ m}\end{align*}$
Due south and due east are perpendicular, so $\triangle ACB$ is right-angled at $C$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);\coordinate (A) at (0,-2);\coordinate (B) at (3.4,0);
\draw (A)--(C)--(B)--cycle;\draw (0,-0.25)--(0.25,-0.25)--(0.25,0);
\path (A) node[below] {$A$} (C) node[above left] {$C$} (B) node[right] {$B$};
\path (0,-1) node[left] {$60\text{ m}$} (1.7,0) node[above] {$60\sqrt{3}\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}AB&=\sqrt{AC^2+BC^2}\\AB&=\sqrt{60^2+(60\sqrt{3})^2}\\AB&=120\text{ m}\end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
A lighthouse has its top $50\text{ m}$ above sea level. From boat $A$, the lighthouse is on a bearing of $060^\circ\text{T}$; from boat $B$, it is on a bearing of $150^\circ\text{T}$. The angle of depression from the top to each boat is $45^\circ$.
Find the distance between the boats to the nearest metre.
The diagram is a top-down view, with $O$ the lighthouse base.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (A) at (-2.6,-1.5);\coordinate (B) at (-1.5,2.6);
\draw (A)--(O)--(B);
\draw[->] (A)--(-2.6,-0.3);\draw[->] (B)--(-1.5,3.8);
\draw (-2.6,-0.8) arc[start angle=90,end angle=30,radius=0.7];
\draw (-1.5,3.3) arc[start angle=90,end angle=-60,radius=0.7];
\path (-2.6,-0.3) node[above] {N} (-1.5,3.8) node[above] {N};
\path (-2.05,-0.65) node {$60^\circ$} (-0.5,2.95) node {$150^\circ$};
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$} (B) node[left] {$B$} (O) node[right] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A vertical tower stands at $C$ on level ground. Observer $P$ is due south of $C$ and observer $Q$ is due east of $C$. The observers are $100\text{ m}$ apart, and the bearing of $Q$ from $P$ is $030^\circ$. The angle of elevation of the tower top $T$ from $Q$ is $45^\circ$.
Find the tower height to the nearest metre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (0,-3);\coordinate (Q) at (1.732,0);
\draw (P)--(C)--(Q)--cycle;\draw (0,-0.25)--(0.25,-0.25)--(0.25,0);
\draw (0,-2.2) arc[start angle=90,end angle=60,radius=0.8];
\path (0.38,-2.05) node {$30^\circ$};
\draw[->] (C)--(0,1);\path (0,1) node[above] {N};
\path (P) node[below] {$P$} (C) node[above left] {$C$} (Q) node[right] {$Q$};
\path (0.866,-1.5) node[below right] {$100\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
In the top-down triangle $PCQ$, the bearing gives $\angle CPQ=30^\circ$. The ground distance $CQ$ is opposite this angle.
$\begin{align*}\sin30^\circ&=\frac{CQ}{100}\\CQ&=100\sin30^\circ\\CQ&=50\text{ m}\end{align*}$
Now use the elevation triangle $QCT$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (Q) at (0,0);\coordinate (C) at (2.5,0);\coordinate (T) at (2.5,2.5);
\draw (Q)--(C)--(T)--cycle;\draw (2.25,0)--(2.25,0.25)--(2.5,0.25);
\path (Q) node[below left] {$Q$} (C) node[below right] {$C$} (T) node[above right] {$T$};
\path (1.25,0) node[below] {$50\text{ m}$} (2.5,1.25) node[right] {$h$} (0.65,0.25) node {$45^\circ$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}\tan45^\circ&=\frac{h}{50}\\h&=50\tan45^\circ\\h&=50\text{ m}\end{align*}$

examples.question_text:
A vertical tower stands at $C$ on level ground. Point $P$ is due south of $C$, and point $Q$ is due east of $C$. The distance $PQ$ is $100\text{ m}$ and the bearing of $Q$ from $P$ is $030^\circ$. The angle of elevation of the tower top $T$ from $P$ is $30^\circ$.
Find the angle of elevation from $Q$ to the nearest degree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (0,-3);\coordinate (Q) at (1.732,0);
\draw (P)--(C)--(Q)--cycle;\draw (0,-0.25)--(0.25,-0.25)--(0.25,0);
\draw (0,-2.2) arc[start angle=90,end angle=60,radius=0.8];
\path (0.38,-2.05) node {$30^\circ$};
\draw[->] (C)--(0,1);\path (0,1) node[above] {N};
\path (P) node[below] {$P$} (C) node[above left] {$C$} (Q) node[right] {$Q$};
\path (0.866,-1.5) node[below right] {$100\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Find both ground distances from the top-down triangle.
$\begin{align*}PC&=100\cos30^\circ\\PC&=50\sqrt{3}\text{ m}\\CQ&=100\sin30^\circ\\CQ&=50\text{ m}\end{align*}$
Use the elevation from $P$ to find the height, keeping the ground distance exact.
$\begin{align*}\tan30^\circ&=\frac{h}{50\sqrt{3}}\\h&=50\sqrt{3}\tan30^\circ\\h&=50\text{ m}\end{align*}$
In $\triangle QCT$, the required angle is $\alpha=\angle TQC$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (Q) at (0,0);\coordinate (C) at (2.5,0);\coordinate (T) at (2.5,2.5);
\draw (Q)--(C)--(T)--cycle;\draw (2.25,0)--(2.25,0.25)--(2.5,0.25);
\draw (0.7,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=45,radius=0.7];
\path (0.95,0.35) node {$\alpha$};
\path (Q) node[below left] {$Q$} (C) node[below right] {$C$} (T) node[above right] {$T$};
\path (1.25,0) node[below] {$50\text{ m}$} (2.5,1.25) node[right] {$50\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*}\tan\alpha&=\frac{50}{50}\\\alpha&=\tan^{-1}(1)\\\alpha&=45^\circ\end{align*}$
